[h2]Fixed: Atlantis, Ragnarok and Eternal Embers no longer appear on the portal page[/h2]

[b]This mod is capped at Immortal Throne, and the travel window finally says so.[/b] If you own the Titan Quest expansions, opening a rebirth fountain or teleport showed act tabs for Atlantis, Ragnarok and Eternal Embers alongside Greece, Egypt, Orient and Immortal Throne. Those acts are not part of this mod and were never meant to be offered.

[list]
[*][b]The portal page now lists exactly four acts:[/b] Greece, Egypt, Orient and Immortal Throne. Every legitimate destination on those four pages is untouched, including Olympus and all of Hades.
[*][b]The quest log lost its DLC act tabs too.[/b] The same record hole put Atlantis, Ragnarok and Eternal Embers tabs in the quest log. They are gone for the same reason.
[*][b]Nothing was removed from the game you own.[/b] This changes only what this mod's act-selection screens offer. Your expansions are untouched outside the mod, and players who own no expansions see no difference at all: they never had those tabs.
[*][b]The cause.[/b] The portal window's page list is a single database record. Soulvizier shipped an Immortal-Throne-era copy of it with four pages, but this port's user-interface cleanup pass deleted that copy, so the base game's own seven-page version took over. The four base pages are now imported back faithfully with the three expansion pages removed.
[*][b]A permanent gate so it cannot come back.[/b] The build now fails loudly if any expansion act reappears on either screen, and equally if one of the four legitimate acts goes missing.
[/list]

[i]This update changes two user-interface records only. No drop rate, loot table, stat, skill, monster or map was touched. The Epic and Legendary soul names, the Boar Snatcher orb, the Spartan Crypt entrance and the chest breadth work from the previous updates are all included.[/i]

[i]Known and being worked on: an Atlantis owner can still reach Atlantis by boat from Rhodes. That voyage is a separate fix and is tracked.[/i]
